{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR-ATTESTED EVIDENCE — the Pass-1 finder runs on OPUS. Criterion SATISFIED.\n\nThe AC asked for a real plan-review run, after the fix, recording opus for the Pass-1 finder, cited\nfrom REBAR_USAGE_LOG per-step attribution. Done, with the var actually exported this time — that\nomission is the only reason the earlier 0d76 run could not be cited.\n\nTHE RUN\n  command   rebar review-plan 5e75-522e-70d1-4363\n  tree      origin/main @ 144bb02251ec052d71fff029b8fce71c4d12cce0\n  verdict   PASS, blocking 0, signed and certified at that sha\n  signed_at 1785701669109051000\n  usage log $CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/usage_run2.jsonl (37 rows)\n\nPER-STEP ATTRIBUTION, aggregated from that log by (step, model_class, model):\n  5 x (finders,            frontier, anthropic:claude-opus-4-8)   <- Pass-1 FINDER on OPUS\n  1 x (verify,             -,        anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6) <- Pass-2\n  1 x (coach_notes,        -,        anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6) <- Pass-4\n  1 x (prerequisite_verify,-,        anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6)\n\nThis is the restoration this ticket argued for, observed end-to-end: Pass-1 resolves the declared\nfrontier class to opus while Pass-2/Pass-4 stay on the standard model — the operator decision\nrecorded on this epic, and the behaviour the sidecar archaeology showed had been absent since\n2026-06-27. The verdict envelope independently reports model=anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6 as the RUN\ncfg, which is the point: the finder no longer inherits it. Before b690 the finder would have taken\nthat sonnet cfg, which is exactly the regression.\n\nThe discrimination is real, not incidental: had req.config still been discarded, every row would\ncarry the run cfg (sonnet) rather than opus, because the run cfg IS sonnet here.\n\nALSO SATISFIED THIS RUN: the prerequisite-window test criterion. Commit cherry-picked onto current\norigin/main (its original parents were SHA-rewritten by Gerrit on submit, so a cherry-pick, not a\nrebase); 6 passed in test_pass1_finder_model.py. Re-mutation-checked ON THIS TREE rather than relying\non the pre-merge proof: forcing model=None at prerequisites.py:187 turns\ntest_the_prerequisite_finder_packs_against_the_frontier_model RED (\"packed against None\"); restoring\nreturns it GREEN."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785702885344046001,"uuid":"d438c41a-1b0c-490a-a374-97bb4f96c734"}